<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Example Site — #code</title><description>Posts tagged with &quot;code&quot; from Example Site</description><link>https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/</link><item><title>Everything at Once</title><link>https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/notes/everything/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/notes/everything/</guid><description>Inline code, an external SVG, tables, maths, callouts, footnotes and citations in one note.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Feb 2025 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;THIS CONTENT IS ENTIRELY LLM WRITTEN&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;drop-cap&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;opening-words&quot;&gt;his note&lt;/span&gt; uses every kind of content the theme sets, so that one page can show how they sit together. &lt;span class=&quot;footnote-sentence&quot;&gt;It is a short working document: a few paragraphs of prose with &lt;code&gt;inline code&lt;/code&gt; in the line, a command such as &lt;code&gt;pnpm exec astro build --root examples/full&lt;/code&gt; that has to wrap with the text around it, and a few notes in the margin.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;footnote&quot; role=&quot;doc-noteref&quot; href=&quot;#fn:inline&quot; id=&quot;fnref:inline&quot; data-footnote-ref aria-describedby=&quot;footnotes&quot; class=&quot;footnote-ref&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;an-external-svg&quot;&gt;An external SVG&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#an-external-svg&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The diagram below is a separate file served from the site, not inline markup. That keeps it cacheable on its own, and it scales with the column whatever the width of the screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://visruthsk.github.io/website-theme/diagram.svg&quot; alt=&quot;Three boxes labelled tell, listen and retell joined by arrows&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;footnote-sentence&quot;&gt;A caption is not needed when the surrounding sentence says what the picture shows, and the alternative text carries the same description for readers who cannot see it.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;footnote&quot; role=&quot;doc-noteref&quot; href=&quot;#fn:svg&quot; id=&quot;fnref:svg&quot; data-footnote-ref aria-describedby=&quot;footnotes&quot; class=&quot;footnote-ref&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;code-tables-and-maths&quot;&gt;Code, tables and maths&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#code-tables-and-maths&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Code blocks are highlighted at build time, so no script runs in the reader’s browser, and the block keeps its own title and copy button:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;expressive-code&quot;&gt;&lt;figure class=&quot;frame has-title&quot;&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;count.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;pre data-language=&quot;ts&quot; class=&quot;wrap&quot; style=&quot;--ecMaxLine:49ch&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ec-line&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gutter&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ln&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;1&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;export&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#6F42C1;--1:#B392F0&quot;&gt;words&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#AE4B07;--1:#FFAB70&quot;&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF&quot;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF&quot;&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; {&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ec-line&quot; style=&quot;--ecIndent:2ch&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gutter&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ln&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;2&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;indent&quot;&gt;  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt; text.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#6F42C1;--1:#B392F0&quot;&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF&quot;&gt;\s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#BF3441;--1:#F97583&quot;&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#032F62;--1:#9ECBFF&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#6F42C1;--1:#B392F0&quot;&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;(Boolean).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#005CC5;--1:#79B8FF&quot;&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ec-line&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;gutter&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ln&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;3&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;code&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;--0:#24292E;--1:#E1E4E8&quot;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;copy&quot;&gt;&lt;div aria-live=&quot;polite&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;button title=&quot;Copy to clipboard&quot; data-copied=&quot;Copied!&quot; data-code=&quot;export function words(text: string): number {  return text.split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length}&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tables line their numbers up on the right and keep the same rhythm as the text above them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Story&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;Words&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;Year&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;The Selfish Giant&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;1,652&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;1888&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;The Frog-Prince&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;1,192&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;1812&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;The Elves and the Shoemaker&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;743&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;text-align: right&quot;&gt;1812&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inline maths such as &lt;math&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow class=&quot;tml-sml-pad&quot;&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;π&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;0&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt; sits in the line, and display maths takes a line of its own:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;math-display&gt;&lt;math display=&quot;block&quot; class=&quot;tml-display&quot; style=&quot;display:block math;&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;munderover&gt;&lt;mo movablelimits=&quot;false&quot;&gt;∑&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;k&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/munderover&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;k&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mfrac&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo fence=&quot;true&quot; form=&quot;prefix&quot; stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;(&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mo fence=&quot;true&quot; form=&quot;postfix&quot; stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;)&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mfrac&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/math-display&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;callouts-quotations-and-citations&quot;&gt;Callouts, quotations and citations&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#callouts-quotations-and-citations&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;details data-callout=&quot;note&quot; open&gt;&lt;summary&gt;&lt;span&gt;Note&lt;span&gt; (Callouts)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/summary&gt;&lt;p&gt;A callout can hold &lt;code&gt;inline code&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://pagefind.app&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;external-link-new-tab-description&quot; data-external=&quot;&quot;&gt;link&lt;span class=&quot;external-link-icon-wrap&quot;&gt;⁠&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and more than one paragraph of text.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;details data-callout=&quot;tip&quot; open&gt;&lt;summary&gt;&lt;span&gt;Tip&lt;span&gt; (Quotations)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/summary&gt;&lt;p&gt;A block quotation keeps the body typeface and is set apart by its rule, as in this sentence from Wilde:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was a large lovely garden, with soft green grass.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Citations are numbered in the order they first appear and link to the reference list at the foot of the page, as with the story quoted above &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot;&gt;[&lt;a href=&quot;#ref-wilde1888&quot; class=&quot;citation-link&quot; aria-label=&quot;1. Wilde, Oscar, 1888. The Happy Prince and Other Tales&quot; data-citation-preview=&quot;Wilde, Oscar (1888). The Happy Prince and Other Tales. David Nutt.&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;. &lt;span class=&quot;footnote-sentence&quot;&gt;A group takes one set of brackets &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot;&gt;[see &lt;a href=&quot;#ref-knuth1984&quot; class=&quot;citation-link&quot; aria-label=&quot;2. Knuth, Donald E., 1984. The TeXbook&quot; data-citation-preview=&quot;Knuth, Donald E. (1984). The TeXbook. Addison-Wesley.&quot;&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;; &lt;a href=&quot;#ref-knuth1981&quot; class=&quot;citation-link&quot; aria-label=&quot;3. Knuth, Donald E., Plass, Michael F., 1981. Breaking Paragraphs into Lines&quot; data-citation-preview=&quot;Knuth, Donald E. &amp;amp; Plass, Michael F. (1981). Breaking Paragraphs into Lines. Software: Practice and Experience, 11(11), 1119–1184.&quot;&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;, and a locator can follow the key.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;footnote&quot; role=&quot;doc-noteref&quot; href=&quot;#fn:citation&quot; id=&quot;fnref:citation&quot; data-footnote-ref aria-describedby=&quot;footnotes&quot; class=&quot;footnote-ref&quot;&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lists keep the same measure and spacing as paragraphs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nested lists indent by a fixed step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ordered lists number their items in the same colour as the text around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The numbers are text, so they need the same contrast as text.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A third item shows the numbers lining up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every one of these features can be switched off in &lt;code&gt;theme.json&lt;/code&gt;, and the build then leaves no trace of it in the output. The second example site does exactly that, so it makes a useful comparison with this page: it has no margin notes, no maths and no citations, and its pages are correspondingly lighter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;section role=&quot;doc-endnotes&quot; data-footnotes class=&quot;footnotes&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 id=&quot;footnotes&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;a data-heading-anchor=&quot;&quot; href=&quot;#footnotes&quot; aria-label=&quot;Link to this section&quot; tabindex=&quot;-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;fn:inline&quot; role=&quot;doc-endnote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A note with &lt;code&gt;inline code&lt;/code&gt; and a &lt;a href=&quot;https://pagefind.app&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;external-link-new-tab-description&quot; data-external=&quot;&quot;&gt;link to the Pagefind site&lt;span class=&quot;external-link-icon-wrap&quot;&gt;⁠&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, set in the margin beside the line that mentions it. &lt;a role=&quot;doc-backlink&quot; href=&quot;#fnref:inline&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 1&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩︎&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;fn:svg&quot; role=&quot;doc-endnote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A longer note, beside the diagram, long enough to wrap onto several lines in the margin so that its line breaks, its width and its alignment with the paragraph can be checked by eye. &lt;a role=&quot;doc-backlink&quot; href=&quot;#fnref:svg&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 2&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩︎&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;fn:citation&quot; role=&quot;doc-endnote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A note with a long unbroken address that has to wrap instead of running out of the margin: &lt;a href=&quot;https://example.com/stories/the-selfish-giant/chapter-one/paragraph-two/sentence-three&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; aria-describedby=&quot;external-link-new-tab-description&quot; data-external=&quot;&quot;&gt;https://example.com/stories/the-selfish-giant/chapter-one/paragraph-two/sentence-three&lt;span class=&quot;external-link-icon-wrap&quot;&gt;⁠&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a role=&quot;doc-backlink&quot; href=&quot;#fnref:citation&quot; data-footnote-backref=&quot;&quot; aria-label=&quot;Back to reference 3&quot; class=&quot;data-footnote-backref footnote-backref&quot;&gt;↩︎&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;
&lt;section class=&quot;bibliography&quot; aria-label=&quot;References&quot;&gt; &lt;h2 id=&quot;references&quot;&gt;References&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;ol class=&quot;bibliography-list&quot;&gt; &lt;li id=&quot;ref-wilde1888&quot; class=&quot;bibliography-entry&quot;&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-authors&quot;&gt; Wilde, Oscar &lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-year&quot;&gt;(1888).&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-title&quot;&gt;The Happy Prince and Other Tales.&lt;/span&gt;     &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-publisher&quot;&gt;David Nutt.&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li id=&quot;ref-knuth1984&quot; class=&quot;bibliography-entry&quot;&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-authors&quot;&gt; Knuth, Donald E. &lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-year&quot;&gt;(1984).&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-title&quot;&gt;The TeXbook.&lt;/span&gt;     &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-publisher&quot;&gt;Addison-Wesley.&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li id=&quot;ref-knuth1981&quot; class=&quot;bibliography-entry&quot;&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-authors&quot;&gt; Knuth, Donald E. &amp;amp; Plass, Michael F. &lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-year&quot;&gt;(1981).&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-title&quot;&gt;Breaking Paragraphs into Lines.&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;em class=&quot;bibliography-journal&quot;&gt;Software: Practice and Experience&lt;/em&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-volume&quot;&gt;, 11&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-issue&quot;&gt;(11)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;bibliography-pages&quot;&gt;, 1119–1184&lt;/span&gt;
.
